  "notes": "The breadth requirement may be fulfilled at the lower-division and/or upper-division level, and the same course may fulfill a chronological and regional requirement simultaneously. Upper division History courses substituted for the lower division requirements may not be applied to the 40 upper division History units required, although the units will apply to the 60 upper division Letters and Science units required for graduation. Up to 4 units of HIST 99 may apply to the lower division major requirements, and 8 units of HIST 199 or any HIST 196 courses (excluding 196SJ) may apply to the upper division major requirements by petition. History 174Q and 196SJ cannot be applied towards the major. At least 2.0 overall UC average in all upper-division major courses and all courses (Prep and UD) for the major. Up to 4 units of any History 196 courses may be taken P/NP for major credit. All other major courses, including those applied to the major from other departments, must be taken for letter grades. With the approval of each department chairperson, up to a total of 8 units may be applied simultaneously to both UD majors.",
